PVD("estonia_vision_2021-2035",{"docs":["","EST Estonia 2035 Development Strategy"],"s":{"1":[[1,"4","2","Long-Term Strategic Planning and Financial Management Coordination","“Estonia 2035” is strategic management tool which enables the coordination of long-term strategic planning and financial management of the country",""],[1,"4","2","Uniform National Development Management Framework","It is a strategy for the uniform management of Estonia’s development that facilitates cooperation between the Riigikogu and the Government of the Republic and strengthens the links between different types of strategic policy documents.",""],[1,"4","2","Estonia 2035 Integration into Government Decision-Making","Estonia’s strategic goals can be achieved when the agreements made in the “Estonia 2035” strategy are taken into consideration in the decision-making processes by the Riigikogu and the Government of the Republic.",""],[1,"4","2","Parliamentary Approval of the Strategy General Part","The general part of the strategy is approved by the Riigikogu at the proposal of the Government of the Republic.",""],[1,"4","3","Sectoral and Local Strategic Planning Implementation Mechanism","The “Estonia 2035” strategy is carried out mainly via sectoral development plans and programmes in the respective fields.",""],[1,"19","6","Annual Action Plan Monitoring and Adjustment Mechanism","Their implementation is monitored on the basis of a more detailed action plan each year and, if necessary, adjustments are made based on domestic events affecting the development of Estonia and changes in the foreign environment.",""],[1,"29","1","Estonia 2035 Strategy Coordination Mechanism","The Government Office is responsible for coordinating the preparation, implementation and amendment of the strategy “Estonia 2035” in cooperation with the Ministry of Finance.","The Government Office | the Ministry of Finance"],[1,"29","1","Development Plan and Programme Implementation Framework","“Estonia 2035” is carried out mainly via development plans and programmes in the respective fields.",""],[1,"29","1","Multi-Stakeholder Contribution to Strategy Implementation","Achieving Estonia’s strategic goals also requires the contribution of local governments and public, non-governmental and private sector organizations, as well as the knowledge of the Estonian people in making everyday choices.",""],[1,"29","2","Cross-Sectoral Alignment of Development Plans and Programmes","All development plans in the field approved by the Government of the Republic and programmes approved by the Minister follow the goals and necessary changes agreed upon in the strategy “Estonia 2035”.",""],[1,"29","2","Streamlined Strategy Implementation Reporting","When reporting on the implementation of the strategy, we consider it important that the load is as light as possible for the parties involved and in accordance with the state budget strategy and activity-based budget.",""],[1,"29","3","EU and SDG Alignment in Development Planning","the development plans and programmes prepared on the basis of “Estonia 2035” will also reflect Estonia's sectoral policy goals of the European Union and issues related to the implementation of global sustainable development goals.",""],[1,"29","3","Estonia 2035 Implementation Review Mechanism","The annual Estonian state report, to be completed within the framework of the European Semester and the published country-specific recommendations, will be an input to the reviews of the implementation of “Estonia 2035”.",""],[1,"29","3","Fiscal Policy Support for Estonia 2035","Achieving the strategic goals of “Estonia 2035” must be supported by the country's fiscal policy decisions.",""]],"2":[[1,"8","2","Higher Education and Research Linkage Reform","higher education and research and development activities must become more closely linked.",""],[1,"20","2","Gender Balance in Higher Education","We will strive for gender balance in higher education.",""],[1,"20","2","Estonian-Language Higher Education and Research Development","We will support the preservation and development of Estonian-language curricula in higher education and the development of Estonian professional and research languages.",""],[1,"20","2","Higher Education Funding and Student Support Reform","We are reviewing the funding model for higher education, including updating the system of student loans, study grants and scholarships.",""],[1,"20","2","Labour-Market Responsive Higher Education","We will ensure that education will respond to the needs of the society and the labour better",""],[1,"20","2","Higher Education and Research Integration","higher education and research and development will be better integrated.",""],[1,"20","3","Higher Education Quality and Funding Efficiency Improvement","We will improve the quality of higher education and increase the efficiency of its funding",""],[1,"27","1","Research Stakeholder Communication Coordination","We need to better coordinate both formal and informal communication between researchers, the public sector, business and the civil society",""],[1,"27","1","Strategic Development of Research Institutions","We will ensure the strategic development of research institutions",""],[1,"27","1","Basic Research Funding","continuing to fund basic research for new knowledge, technologies, and ideas",""],[1,"27","1","Research Community and Infrastructure Development","advocating for the growth of the research community, and enabling high-quality research infrastructure",""],[1,"27","1","International Research Cooperation","participating in the international knowledge community",""],[1,"27","1","Researcher Working Conditions and Career Support","We will provide competitive working conditions and career opportunities for researchers",""],[1,"27","1","Academic Career and Doctoral Studies Reform","We elaborate an academic career model that supports researchers' diversified development and offers greater stability",""],[1,"27","1","Researcher Labour Mobility Programme","We will facilitate the labour mobility between universities, business and the public sector",""],[1,"27","1","Shared Research Infrastructure Access","open up research infrastructure for both enterprises and the public sector",""],[1,"27","1","University Knowledge Transfer Services Improvement","improve the quality of university knowledge transfer services",""],[1,"27","1","Open Science and Research Results Dissemination","We will improve the wider availability and use of research results",""],[1,"27","1","Knowledge-Based Thinking and Citizen Science Support","support the spread of knowledge-based thinking in society, including civil science",""],[1,"27","1","Estonian Nation, Language and Culture Research Support","We will support Estonian research and scientific work that deals with the study of the Estonian nation, language, culture, identity, and self-awareness",""],[1,"27","1","Language Technology Development and Implementation","We will ensure the development of language technology solutions and encourage their widest possible implementation",""]],"3":[[1,"16","2","Private-Sector R&D and Innovation Support","Favourable conditions have been created for R&D and innovation in private sector",""],[1,"23","6","Business Research and Innovation Support Solutions","We will introduce new solutions to encourage research and development and innovation in business sector",""],[1,"23","7","Business Innovation Support Services","We will develop new support services to encourage innovation in all stages of the business and technology development",""],[1,"23","7","Applied Research Support Reorganisation","We will also reorganise support for applied research",""],[1,"23","7","State-Owned Company Research Investment","increase investment in research and development by state-owned companies",""],[1,"23","7","Research Knowledge Commercialisation Acceleration","We will facilitate the scientific knowledge created in Estonian research institutions to advance to business use faster",""],[1,"23","7","Research Institution and Enterprise Collaboration","we will encourage collaboration between research institutions and entrepreneurs",""],[1,"24","1","Business and Technology R&D and Innovation Support","support R&D and innovation at all stages of business and technology development, and take into account the regional differences.",""],[1,"24","5","Sectoral Research Programmes for R&D Collaboration","we will develop sectoral research programmes",""],[1,"24","5","Reassessment of Smart Specialisation Priorities","rethink smart specialisation priorities",""],[1,"24","5","Support for Participation in European Strategic Value Chains","provide support for participation in the European Union’s strategic value chains",""],[1,"24","5","Sustainable Bio-Economy Promotion Initiative","promote a sustainable bio-economy",""],[1,"24","7","Integrated Public-Private Research and Innovation System","We will shape the Estonian research and development and innovation system into a well-functioning integrated whole, where the research and development activities of private and the public sector are closely intertwined and support each other.",""],[1,"24","7","Enterprise Digitisation and Automation Support","We will support the digitisation and automation of enterprises",""],[1,"24","7","Enterprise Data Quality and Real-Time Exchange Mechanism","ensure data quality that enables real-time data exchange between enterprises and in communication with the state",""],[1,"24","7","Knowledge-Intensive Enterprise Business Diplomacy","in business diplomacy we will focus on knowledge-intensive enterprises",""],[1,"24","7","Regional Economic Structural Change Facilitation","we will facilitate the acceleration of structural changes in the economy outside Harju County",""]],"4":[[1,"9","5","Green Resource Valorisation and Technology Development","Greater emphasis must be placed on environment-friendly technologies and business models and on greater and greener valorisation of local resources and secondary raw materials.",""],[1,"24","1","Environment-Friendly and Sustainable Entrepreneurship Promotion","We will promote environment-friendly and sustainable entrepreneurship through new legislation and other activities needed, ensuring a balance between the expectations of entrepreneurs and consumers.",""],[1,"24","3","Circular Economy Principles Introduction","We will introduce the principles of the circular economy",""],[1,"24","8","Sustainable Production and Consumption Promotion","we will encourage the introduction of sustainable production and consumption patterns.",""],[1,"24","8","Enterprise Resource and Energy Efficiency Support","Enterprises need to improve resource efficiency, including energy efficiency, for example, through industrial symbiosis, digitisation and support for more resource-efficient technologies.",""],[1,"24","8","Waste Management and Material Recycling Reform","We are reorganising waste management based on the waste hierarchy and introducing innovative solutions to reduce waste generation and increase material recycling and separate waste collection.",""]],"5":[[1,"11","7","Energy Infrastructure Security and Supply Development","In the case of energy infrastructure, energy security and security of supply issues need to be addressed.",""],[1,"25","1","Climate-Neutral Energy Production and Security Transition","We will move to climate-neutral energy production, ensuring energy security",""],[1,"25","7","Renewable Energy Expansion and Offshore Wind Support","In order to increase the share of renewable energy, we will find a solution that takes into account security, environmental protection and the interests of the population.",""],[1,"25","7","Socio-Economic Mitigation for Oil Shale Phase-Out","we will support the mitigation of the socio-economic impacts of reduced electricity production from oil shale during the transition period",""],[1,"25","7","Ida-Viru Fair Transition Services and Investment Package","develop and implement a package of services and investments for Ida-Viru County that will help its people, enterprises and local governments benefit from the changes and ensure a fair transition to the new economy.",""]],"6":[[1,"11","6","Historic City Centre Compaction Initiative","Where possible, historic city centres should be compacted.",""],[1,"11","6","Integrated State Spatial Planning Capacity Reform","Greater state competence is needed for integrated spatial planning in order to ensure, among other things, coherence between state and local government investments, and to adapt to demographic changes and other development needs.",""],[1,"11","6","Spatial Planning Competence and Data Services Initiative","To make better spatial decisions, we need to increase everyone's spatial planning competence, supported by high-quality spatial data and smarter services.",""],[1,"17","1","Inclusive Spatial Planning and Design","decisions are based on the basic principles of high-quality space planning and the principles of inclusive design to ensure that everyone has access to, and finds comfort in, the mental, physical and digital space.",""],[1,"17","1","Technology and Nature-Based Living Environment Solutions","Innovative technologies and nature-based solutions are used, reducing the time spent covering distances and ensuring a good living environment in every part of Estonia.",""],[1,"17","2","Safe and Accessible Public Space Planning","when planning public space, preference is given to solutions that promote safe and secure and health-promoting behaviours that ensure accessibility.",""],[1,"25","3","Comprehensive Spatial Planning and Renovation","We plan and renovate the space comprehensively and with high-quality, while also taking into account the needs of society, demographic changes, health and care for the environment",""],[1,"25","4","High-Quality and Accessible Spatial Planning","In spatial planning decisions, we will follow the principles of high-quality space creation: high-quality space combines artistic, technological and economic solutions and the natural environment into a balanced whole.",""],[1,"25","4","Regionally Balanced Spatial Planning Development","We will ensure comprehensive and regionally balanced spatial planning development of the state, where the investments of the state and local governments are in harmony.",""],[1,"25","4","Compact Settlement Adaptation Programme","We will introduce well-thought-out spatial solutions to adapt to population changes, and in the conditions of a shrinking population, we will adjust the settlements to be more compact.",""],[1,"25","4","Safe Public Space Planning","When planning public space, we are broadly introducing the principles of creating a safe space to promote safe and secure behaviour.",""],[1,"25","4","Health-Promoting and Accessible Public Space Solutions","We will support solutions that increase physical activity, promote health and ensure accessibility.",""],[1,"25","4","Spatial Planning Capacity Development","We will increase the competence of space creation.",""],[1,"25","4","National Building Stock Renovation Plan","We will improve the quality and availability of the building stock through a long-term national renovation plan.",""],[1,"25","4","Climate-Resilient Urban Settlement Solutions","We will introduce solutions that increase the resilience of urban settlements to the effects of climate change.",""],[1,"25","4","Sustainable Waste Management Development","We will develop sustainable waste management.",""],[1,"25","4","Public Water Supply and Sewerage Infrastructure","We will develop sustainable waste management, public water supply and sewerage infrastructure.",""],[1,"25","4","Sustainable Mineral Resource Mapping and Use","We will also map and sustainably use mineral resources.",""]],"7":[[1,"11","7","Healthy and Sustainable Mobility Environment Development","We need to make living, studying, leisure and working environments and the movement between them more healthy and supportive of environment-friendly and safe choices, as well as more accessible to all members of the society.",""],[1,"11","7","European External Transport Connections Development","The development of external land transport connections must continue in line with the European Union’s plan to build a core transport network (including Via Baltica and Rail Baltic).",""],[1,"26","5","Clean Vehicle Infrastructure Development","We are creating the infrastructure to switch to clean vehicles",""],[1,"26","5","Public Sector Clean Vehicle Uptake","increasing the use of clean vehicles in the public sector",""],[1,"26","5","International and National Transport Connections","developing international and national connections to reduce the time required to cover distances",""],[1,"26","5","Road Safety and Accessibility Improvement","increasing road safety and accessibility",""],[1,"26","5","Hydrogen and New Transport Technology Support","We are open and support new technologies, such as the use of hydrogen",""],[1,"26","5","European Electricity Grid Synchronisation","we will synchronise the electricity grid with the continental European frequency band",""],[1,"26","5","Renewable Energy Grid Connection Development","create the necessary grid connections for renewable energy production",""],[1,"26","5","Smart Grid and Energy Storage Deployment","deploy smart grids, short-term and long-term storage options",""],[1,"26","6","Sustainable Transport and Energy Infrastructure Investment","We will implement a safe, environmental-friendly, competitive, needs-based and sustainable transport and energy infrastructure",""],[1,"26","8","Needs-Based Interoperable Transport Service","We will provide a needs-based interoperable transport service that includes all means of transportation",""],[1,"26","9","Integrated Mobility Data Transport Model","To ensure the integration and mobility of transportation across Estonia, we will develop and implement a model that takes into account the socio-economic and environmental factors.",""],[1,"26","9","Public and Shared Transport Promotion","At the same time, we will promote the use of public and shared transport and a healthy and sustainable means of mobility.",""]],"8":[[1,"12","3","Participatory Democracy Expansion","One of the important mechanisms for strengthening civil society and building a cohesive society is the wider spread of participatory democracy.",""],[1,"12","3","Public-Sector Labour and Service Cooperation","the public sector will also need to target its labour resources wisely and work with the private and civil sectors because the need for public services will not diminish.",""],[1,"12","3","Bureaucracy Reduction","This requires, among other things, the reduction of bureaucracy",""],[1,"12","3","Co-Creative Policy-Making with Civil Society","co-creative policy-making with people and civil society",""],[1,"12","3","Public Service Role Agreement","an agreement on the role of the state, local governments and the community in the provision of public services",""],[1,"12","5","Intergovernmental Cooperation and Public Consultation Mechanism","Cooperation between the central government, local governments, and communities and wider public consultation in finding solutions based on people’s needs",""],[1,"12","5","Clear Division of Implementation Roles","a clear division of roles in their implementation",""],[1,"12","5","Local Government Financial Capacity Support","ensuring the financial capacity of local governments",""],[1,"12","5","Public Initiatives and Citizen Survey Programme","organizing more extensive public initiatives and surveys at the initiative of both the state and citizens",""],[1,"26","1","Needs-Based and Flexible Governance Reform","For this, we will make governance more needs-based and flexible.",""],[1,"26","1","Regional Public-Service Workforce Skills Programme","We will ensure staff and officials (e.g., teachers, health workers, rescuers, police officers, prison officers, legal professionals) possessing the necessary skills for the state, taking into account regional needs (including remote and declining areas).",""],[1,"26","1","Organisational Adaptability Development","We develop organisations and people to adapt to changes in global trends",""],[1,"26","1","State and Local Government Strategic Planning","We develop organisations and people to adapt to changes in global trends, but also strategic planning at both the state and local government entity level.",""],[1,"26","1","Digital Country and Data Economy Development","We will also promote Estonia as a digital country, and develop data economy.",""],[1,"26","1","Cybersecurity Development Programme","Considering the growth of cyber threats and geopolitical changes, we will develop cyber security in various areas both in Estonia and in the European Union as a whole",""],[1,"26","1","Cybercrime Detection and Processing Solutions","introduce sustainable solutions to increase the detection of cybercrime and process it more efficiently",""],[1,"26","1","Critical Services and Infrastructure Viability Improvement","improve the viability of critical services and infrastructure.",""],[1,"26","1","Youth Civic Participation Initiative","We will support young people's active civic participation and their connection to the Estonian state.",""],[1,"26","2","State and Local Government Service Quality Improvement","We will improve the quality and availability of state and local government entity services",""],[1,"26","2","Government Responsibility Division Review","review the division of responsibilities",""],[1,"26","7","State and Local Service Responsibility Review","we will review the division of responsibilities between the state and local levels in the provision of services.",""],[1,"26","7","Decentralization and Regional Cooperation Initiative","we will strengthen the partnership between the state and local governments and increase the role of local governments by promoting decentralization and regional cooperation.",""],[1,"26","7","Public Sector Partnership Development","We will also develop public sector cooperation with the private sector, NGOs and communities.",""],[1,"27","6","User-Centred Public Services and Multilingual Support","When designing public services, we will aim to make the user experience as simple and supportive as possible (incl. by offering user support in Estonian and, if necessary, in other common languages).",""],[1,"27","6","Secure Data-Enabled Public Service Delivery","We will make the services as functional and predictable as possible in the background, using all the data available in the state securely and taking into account the human will and fundamental rights.",""],[1,"27","6","Single-Point Physical and Digital Service Access","We will apply the principle of a single place of business in both physical and digital space.",""],[1,"27","6","Justice System and Rights Enforcement Reform","We will develop the justice system and improve the enforcement of rights based on the rule of law.",""]],"9":[[1,"11","5","Cultural Participation and Multilingual Access Support","cultivation of one’s own culture ... and the availability of world culture in different languages – must be supported",""],[1,"25","6","Inclusive Cultural Participation and Cooperation Initiative","We will ensure participation opportunities, joint activities and the availability of various cultural events both for Estonians and people with other mother tongues, promoting cooperation, flexibility and creative solutions of various institutions and organisations, such as job offers, flexible transport, teleworking, cooperation with the private sector, etc.",""],[1,"25","6","Cultural Development and Leadership Recognition Initiative","We will create opportunities for maintaining and developing our own culture and acknowledge the leaders in the field of culture.",""],[1,"25","6","Digital Culture Technology and Content Reuse Initiative","We will adopt new technologies to improve the quality of the creation, preservation and accessibility of digital culture, diversify business services and facilitate the new and cross-use of digital content.",""]],"10":[[1,"19","2","Integrated Secondary Education Reform","To this end, we will integrate formal and non-formal education and general and vocational secondary education and develop a common secondary education standard.",""],[1,"19","2","School Network Optimisation","We will continue to optimise the school network",""],[1,"19","2","Regional Education Centres","create regional education centres with the aim of providing new forms of learning and opportunities for connecting general, vocational and higher education and non-formal learning, including youth work, and facilitating such transitions.",""],[1,"19","2","Future Competencies and Practical Skills Curriculum Reform","We will increase the teaching of general and future competencies in the curricula of different levels and types of education, and integrate more practical experience and skills into them in cooperation with employers.",""],[1,"19","2","Nationwide Quality Youth Work","We will guarantee high-quality youth work available throughout Estonia, which creates opportunities for all young people to gain diverse development, success, experience, and independence.",""],[1,"19","2","Estonian-Language Teaching Support","We will support teaching in Estonian",""],[1,"19","2","Digital Learning Materials in Estonian","developing digital teaching materials in Estonian at all levels of education and in lifelong learning.",""],[1,"19","2","Personalised and Digital Learning Methods","We will support evidence-based development and implementation of diverse learning methods and techniques (including digital pedagogy) in order to personalise and individualise learning and enrich it with technology (learning analytics, kratts, etc.).",""],[1,"19","2","European Education Mobility Facilitation","We will ensure that the learning movement in the European education area is free of obstacles.",""],[1,"19","2","Foreign Language Learning Support","International mobility and cooperation are enhanced by the population’s knowledge of foreign languages, which is why the learning of languages is supported.",""],[1,"19","2","Estonian Language and Digital Learning for Non-Residents","we will provide opportunities to learn the Estonian language and (digital) solutions for compatriots living elsewhere and other interested people.",""],[1,"20","1","Talented Learner Identification and Support System","we create a whole system for noticing and supporting a talented learner",""],[1,"20","1","Integrated Science Technology and Creativity Learning","we expand and promote integrated learning opportunities in science, technology and creativity",""],[1,"20","1","Teacher Capacity Expansion Across Education Levels","we ensure the proliferation of teachers needed to teach them at all levels of education, as well as in hobby education",""],[1,"20","5","Future Work Curriculum Development","We will develop curricula to shape the knowledge and skills needed for future work",""],[1,"20","5","Teacher, Lecturer and Trainer Readiness Development","increase the readiness of teachers, lecturers and trainers",""],[1,"20","5","Modernisation of Learning Environments","modernise learning environments for the implementation of updated curricula",""]],"11":[[1,"20","2","Work-Based Learning Expansion","we will expand work-based learning",""],[1,"20","2","Industrial PhD and Business Master’s Studies","industrial PhD and master’s degree studies in business",""],[1,"20","2","Higher Education Internship System Improvement","improve the internship system",""],[1,"20","7","Adult Education System Modernisation Programme","We will modernise the adult education system (incl. development of a combined funding model and quality assurance principles, changes in tax and support systems, involvement of a network of cultural institutions) to prepare people for future work and adaptation to structural changes in the economy.",""],[1,"20","7","Skills and Needs Forecasting System","We will develop a skills and needs forecasting system (OSKA) and will be able to use big data to better match education and labour market needs.",""],[1,"20","7","Partial Qualifications Certification System","In higher and vocational education, we are developing a system of certification of partial qualifications",""],[1,"20","7","Advanced Skills and Future Competencies Learning Expansion","We will also expand learning opportunities for people with higher skill levels and education, paying attention to areas of smart specialisation and general and future competencies.",""]],"12":[[1,"8","2","Education and Labour Market Alignment Reform","The match between education and the needs of society and the labour market must be improved on all levels of education.",""],[1,"20","5","Future Work Regulatory and Social Protection Reform","We will design the tax system, labour law and social protection rules to comply with the new forms of work, so that they will also ensure equal treatment for, for example, creative freelancers, workbits and via platforms (including cross-border employees) employees.",""],[1,"20","5","Teleworking Opportunities Support","support teleworking opportunities",""],[1,"20","5","Modernisation of Working Environments and Digital Infrastructure","modernise the working environment (including digital infrastructure)",""],[1,"20","5","Workplace Safety Across Employment Forms","ensure safety regardless of the form of work",""],[1,"20","7","Labour Market Return Support Programme","The focus is on more effective support for the return to the labour market of unskilled and inactive people (including the elderly, young people not in education, training or employment, people with a care burden)",""],[1,"20","7","Older Worker Labour Market Retention Measures","the prevention of older people leaving the labour market.",""],[1,"21","8","Local Workforce Participation Support","develop solutions that would keep the local population active in the Estonian labour market",""],[1,"21","8","Estonian Return Facilitation Measures","We will also pay greater attention to facilitating the return to Estonia.",""],[1,"21","8","Pay Gap Reduction Measures","develop measures to support the minimisation of the pay gap",""],[1,"21","8","Reduction of Gender Segregation in Education and Labour","reduce gender segregation in education and the labour market",""]],"13":[[1,"21","2","Comprehensive Population and Family Policy","we are developing a comprehensive population and family policy that supports births and parenthood",""],[1,"21","3","Comprehensive Population and Family Policy","We will develop a comprehensive population and family policy to ensure the sustainability and well-being of the Estonian people",""],[1,"21","2","Intergenerational Cohesion and Active Ageing Initiative","We encourage the change of societal attitudes to value intergenerational cohesion and support the social activism and dignified aging of older people (for example, their greater contribution to volunteer work).",""],[1,"6","3","Immigrant Adaptation and Integration Programme","targeted adaptation and integration of immigrants into the Estonian language and cultural space",""],[1,"6","3","Sustainable Population and Family Support Policy","These demographic changes require a sustainable population policy, a supportive environment for children, youth, education, family and health policies",""],[1,"6","3","Employment Indicators and Longer Working Lives Initiative","development of indicators to promote a high level of employment, longer working lives for the elderly",""],[1,"6","3","Dignified Aging Support","support for dignified aging",""],[1,"6","3","Social and Cultural Participation Initiative","participation of the people living in Estonia and our compatriots in social and cultural activities",""],[1,"6","3","Regional Balanced Development and Rural Liferegion Support","A balanced knowledge-based approach that takes into account regional specificities and needs, reduces socio-economic inequalities in different regions, and supports rural liferegions will help to cope with the urbanisation and demographic changes",""],[1,"8","4","Estonian Language and Culture Learning Opportunities","more efficient opportunities are created for Estonian permanent residents who speak some other language as their mother tongue, as well as compatriots living elsewhere to acquire Estonian and get to know Estonian culture",""],[1,"21","8","Adaptation and Integration Services Modernisation","we will modernise adaptation and integration services",""],[1,"21","8","Inclusive Education and Language Learning Reform","organisation of education and language learning for learners with a mother tongue other than Estonian",""],[1,"21","8","Inclusive Education Development","we will develop inclusive education",""]],"14":[[1,"21","2","Positive Parenting and Child Abuse Prevention Solutions","we are working with state and local government entities to create solutions that support positive parenting and prevent child abuse",""],[1,"21","2","Child Protection and Special Needs Support Reform","update child protection arrangements and support systems for children with special needs",""],[1,"21","2","Services for Children with Complex Problems","develop services for children with complex problems",""],[1,"21","2","Transition to Family-Based Care","continue the transition to family-based care",""]],"15":[[1,"21","5","Integrated Health Prevention and Counselling Measures","To this end, we plan both integrated prevention measures and counselling services for people in a cross-sectoral and inclusive manner.",""],[1,"21","5","Community-Based Health Cooperation Network","We will use permanent forms of cooperation based on a community-based approach and networking.",""],[1,"21","5","Digital Health Education and Risk Behaviour Reduction","Improving the health education of the population and reducing risk behaviour is also supported by the development of digital solutions.",""],[1,"21","5","Healthy Lifestyle Promotion Programme","In addition to promoting healthy lifestyle choices (including a balanced diet, adequate physical and mental activity and social interaction)",""],[1,"21","5","Primary Education for Healthy Living Environments","We will increase people’s awareness of the living environment starting from primary education because it directly affects people’s health in society at large.",""],[1,"21","5","Product, Chemical, Water and Medicine Safety Assurance","We will ensure the safety of products and chemicals, drinking water, medicines",""],[1,"21","5","High-Quality Food Availability Improvement","improve the availability of high-quality food.",""],[1,"21","6","Health and Environmental Protection Behaviour Initiative","We will shape the living environment and people's attitudes and behaviour to be more protective of health and the environment, and reduce risk behaviour",""]],"16":[[1,"23","8","Health Professional Training Programme","training health professionals",""],[1,"22","1","Integrated Health and Social Services","We will integrate health and social services in a people-centered way",""],[1,"22","2","Personalized Medicine Integration in Healthcare","We will integrate personal medicine solutions into the daily activities of the healthcare system",""],[1,"22","9","Personalized Medicine Integration in Healthcare","In order to prolong healthy life years, we will integrate personal medicine solutions into the daily activities of the healthcare system, including the inclusion of human genetic and health data in evidence-based decision-making processes in both treatment and prevention.",""],[1,"23","5","Health Insurance and Healthcare Financing Sustainability","We will ensure that people have adequate health insurance coverage and the sustainability of health care financing",""],[1,"23","8","Personalized Preventive Health Services","We will develop services that take into account human health behaviour, environmental and genetic data, and therefore enable individuals, including doctors, to better prevent disease, monitor health and treatment.",""],[1,"23","8","Digital Health Solutions Development","we will support the development of appropriate digital solutions",""],[1,"23","8","International Health Data Exchange Mechanism","enhancing data exchange (including between countries)",""],[1,"23","8","Health Data and Services Research Programme","research in the respective field",""],[1,"23","8","Health Data Legal Environment Update","updating the legal environment",""],[1,"23","8","Health Data Use Regulation","regulating data use",""]],"17":[[1,"23","1","Social Protection Organisation Modernisation","We will modernise the organisation of social protection, taking into account the changes in the society",""],[1,"23","2","Integrated Services Coordination for Special Needs","Health, employment and social protection and services in the cultural sector ... must be coordinated and connected in order to improve, inter alia, the well-being of people with special needs.",""],[1,"23","2","Early Detection and Care Assessment System","We are developing a system of appropriate services, including the introduction of the principle of early detection and the creation of assessment systems and tools.",""],[1,"23","2","Home and Community-Based Care Services","We will develop care services that enable to care and support services to be received mainly at home and in the community.",""],[1,"23","2","Social Care Infrastructure Modernisation","We will ... invest in the modernisation of infrastructure.",""],[1,"23","2","Technology and Innovation for Social Services","We will ... support the use of technology and innovative solutions in the social sector.",""],[1,"23","2","Long-Term Care Workforce Training","To this end, we will increase the number of employees in the field of long-term care and improve their qualifications through training and work-based learning.",""],[1,"23","3","Special Needs Well-Being and Social Participation Programme","We will improve the well-being and social activity of people with special needs",""],[1,"23","3","Long-Term Care System Efficiency Reform","improve the efficiency of the long-term care system",""],[1,"23","5","Old-Age and Earned Pension Systems Reform","we will change the system of old-age pensions on favourable terms and the system of earned pension years",""],[1,"23","5","Pension Saving Promotion","promote saving for pension",""],[1,"23","5","Occupational Pension Expansion","promote the use of occupational pensions",""],[1,"23","5","Public Financial Awareness Promotion","increase people’s financial awareness",""],[1,"23","5","Flexible Unemployment and Social Protection Reform","more flexible unemployment and redundancy benefit schemes and the adjustment of social protection schemes",""],[1,"23","5","Needs-Based Social Protection Responsibility Framework","We will agree on the division of responsibilities between the individual, the state and local government entities",""],[1,"23","5","Long-Term Care Financing Model Update","we will update the financing model for long-term care",""]],"18":[[1,"22","5","Occupational Health System Modernisation","We will modernise the occupational health system to support health and reduce people’s incapacity for work",""],[1,"22","7","Comprehensive Mental Health Support System","In order to develop a comprehensive mental health support system, we will agree on common principles and measures and ensure the availability and quality of necessary services throughout the person’s life cycle.",""],[1,"22","7","Mental Health Early Detection and Community Support","We will develop an early detection system and enhance the role of the family and community as a preventive and supportive response to both mental health problems and violence, so that people have the knowledge and skills to reduce mental health risks and recognise risks (e.g., risk of a burnout) and mental health problems as they arise and know when and where to seek help.",""],[1,"22","7","Evidence-Based Violence and Risk Behaviour Prevention Programmes","We are expanding our various evidence-based prevention and social programmes to help prevent and reduce bullying at school or work, harassment in the workplace and other communities, domestic and sexual violence, as well as reducing risk behaviours, raising awareness, and preventing extremist behaviour and radicalisation.",""],[1,"22","7","Network-Based Assistance for Violence Victims","We will develop network-based assistance for victims of violence and measures to help prevent the recurrence of violence.",""],[1,"22","7","Mental Health Support to Prevent Illegal Behaviour","We will also pay attention to solving the mental problems that cause illegal behaviour, including in prisons.",""],[1,"22","8","Mental Health Support Programme","We will support mental health",""],[1,"22","8","Mental and Physical Violence Reduction Initiative","reduce mental and physical violence",""],[1,"22","4","Innovative Occupational Health and Safety Services","We will develop innovative and effective occupational health and safety services, including targeted information and counselling services and information technology solutions that promote occupational health and safety.",""],[1,"22","4","Occupational Health Service Quality Improvement","We will also improve the quality and availability of occupational health services.",""],[1,"22","4","Temporary Work Incapacity Labour Market Retention System","We will develop a system to help people with temporary incapacity for work to remain in the labour market, to prevent their permanent incapacity for work.",""],[1,"22","4","Workplace Risk Factor Awareness Initiative","We will increase the awareness of labour market participants about various risk factors (incl. mental health risk factors, work bullying, and harassment).",""]],"19":[[1,"9","3","E-Residency Programme Development","the e-residency programme ... should be further developed to become an international hub for talent and business",""],[1,"9","3","European Single Market Functioning Improvement","we must actively work to ensure its even better functioning",""],[1,"9","6","Digital Competency Development Programme","it is important to prepare people for the use of technologies and to improve their digital competency.",""],[1,"24","1","Estonia Digital Hub and E-Residency Development","We will turn Estonia into a digital hub to which people from all over the world will come both virtually as e-residents and physically to offer their services to the world and establish enterprises.",""],[1,"24","1","Legislation and Tax Environment for New Business Models","At the same time, we will create legislation and a tax environment that enables the implementation of new business models (e.g., platform economy, social entrepreneurship) and new forms of work, both in Estonia and in the European Union.",""],[1,"24","1","Business Bureaucracy Reduction","We will reduce bureaucratic obstacles to businesses.",""],[1,"24","2","Secure Economic Environment for Responsible Entrepreneurship","We will create a secure economic environment conducive to flexible, innovative and responsible entrepreneurship and fair competition.",""]],"20":[[1,"9","5","Enterprise Long-Term Investment Risk-Sharing Mechanism","The state can help by sharing the risks of companies' long-term investments",""],[1,"9","5","Strategic State Investment Planning","The state can help by ... planning state investments, especially when the investment activity of enterprises has suffered setbacks.",""],[1,"24","1","Banking and Capital Market Development","We are further developing the banking and capital markets in order to improve the ability to cope with crises and provide better financing opportunities for companies in all regions.",""],[1,"24","1","Economic Security Threat Awareness-Raising","We are raising public and private awareness of the threats to economic security.",""]],"21":[[1,"10","3","Marine Environmental Protection and Sustainable Use Measures","more attention needs to be paid to environmental protection measures that also improve the state of the sea and promote economic activity in the use of the sea (e.g., algae and shellfish farming, reed processing).",""]],"22":[[1,"11","4","Crisis Awareness and Preparedness Programme","raise the awareness of state authorities, local authorities and vital service providers about potential threats and to improve their preparedness for crises",""],[1,"11","4","Community-Based Public Safety Services","ensuring the availability of public safety services is effective only in closer cooperation with the community and by using smart solutions",""],[1,"11","4","Cultural Cohesion and Knowledge-Based Public Space","ensuring a strong cultural space that promotes cohesion and knowledge-based public space that supports communication",""],[1,"11","4","Broad Security Concept Implementation","the broad security concept needs to be implemented further",""],[1,"11","4","Allied and Partner Country Cooperation","close relations with the allies and partner countries need to be maintained",""],[1,"11","4","International Institutions and International Law Cooperation","in cooperation with them, functioning of international organisations and efficacy of international law must be ensured",""],[1,"11","4","Cross-Sectoral Security Cooperation","Further cross-sectoral cooperation is also important for security",""],[1,"15","2","Independent and Collective Defence Capability","Estonian national defence is ensured by independent defence capability and collective defence, which is supported by a strong will to defend.",""],[1,"15","2","Broad-Based National Defence Participation","The basis for the organisation of Estonian national defence is a broad concept – everyone must contribute to national defence.",""]],"23":[[1,"12","4","Research-Informed Policy-Making Capacity Reform","The country’s capacity to use research to bring about the necessary change and to involve researchers in policy-making needs to be improved.",""],[1,"12","4","Development Needs-Oriented Research Policy","It is important that research stems more from Estonia’s development needs than before.",""],[1,"12","4","Innovative Solutions and Real-Time Data Exchange Policy","There should be a clear preference for innovative solutions and technologies and for more efficient communication between authorities (and enterprises), based more on real-time data exchange and greater use of open and large data.",""],[1,"12","4","Digital Services Sustainability Strengthening","The quality of services is uneven and the sustainability of digital solutions needs to be strengthened.",""],[1,"12","4","E-Services Infrastructure Security and Continuity Investment","We must constantly contribute to the development of the basic infrastructure and create new alternatives to the existing solutions in case of technological possibilities.",""]],"24":[[1,"6","8","Climate Change Health and Safety Preparedness","improve our preparedness to cope with the effects of climate change on human health, well-being, safety, and the living environment",""],[1,"6","8","Communicable Disease and Pandemic Preparedness","institutions in all fields, and society as a whole, need to be better prepared to prevent the spread of infectious diseases",""]],"25":[[1,"27","3","International Strengths Promotion Initiative","We will focus on sharing Estonia’s strengths with the world, building on Estonia’s achievements in digital, cultural, sports and other fields",""],[1,"27","3","Balanced Tourism Development Policy","providing a positive experience for Estonian guests and using the balanced impact of tourism on the local culture and environment",""],[1,"27","3","Foreign Investment Screening Mechanism","we conduct more in-depth screening of significant foreign investments quickly and transparently",""],[1,"27","3","Foreign Language Skills Development","Improving Estonia’s international position is supported by the foreign language skills of the Estonian population",""],[1,"27","3","Development Cooperation Effectiveness Programme","We will increase the effectiveness of development cooperation in order to build peaceful societies in the world",""],[1,"27","3","Crisis Preparedness and Hybrid Threat Resilience Programme","We will develop the broad concept of security and improve society’s crisis preparedness and resilience to hybrid threats",""],[1,"27","3","Treaty-Based International Relations and Alliance Strengthening","Estonia will do its utmost to develop treaty-based international relations, strengthen the European Union and NATO, and develop friendly relations with allies",""],[1,"27","3","Allied Presence Infrastructure Development","We will develop the necessary infrastructure for the presence of our allies",""],[1,"27","3","Responsive Military Service Organisation","make the organisation of military service more responsive to people’s abilities",""],[1,"27","3","Illegal Migration Prevention and Processing Mechanism","In cooperation with the private and civil sectors, we will improve the prevention, detection and processing of illegal migration",""],[1,"27","3","Constitutional Order and Hybrid Threat Resilience","We will increase our resilience to threats to the constitutional order, including hybrid threats and subversion",""],[1,"27","3","Vital Services Security and Community Responsibility Programme","We will secure the functioning of vital services and increase the responsibility of communities in ensuring security and preventing crime",""],[1,"27","3","Community Security and National Defence Awareness","increasing people’s awareness of their role in national defence and ensuring community security",""],[1,"27","3","Technology-Enabled Security Service Improvement","we will make security-enhancing services more effective through technical and innovative solutions",""],[1,"27","3","Cyber Risk Management and Reliable Cyberspace","We will ensure that the cyber risks of the digital society are well managed and that Estonian cyberspace is highly reliable",""]],"26":[[1,"29","8","National Reform Programme Submission to the European Commission","Submitting the National Reform Programme to the European Commission",""],[1,"29","8","Government Cabinet Strategy Discussion","Strategy discussion in the Government Cabinet",""],[1,"29","8","Government Action Plan Update","Updating the Action Plan of the Government of the Republic",""],[1,"29","8","Spring Economic Forecast","Spring economic forecast",""],[1,"29","9","Strategy Discussion with Partners and Interest Groups","Strategy discussion with partners and interest groups",""],[1,"29","10","State Budget Strategy and Budget Preparation","Preparing the state budget strategy and the state budget",""],[1,"29","10","Strategy Day with Partners and Interest Groups","Strategy day with partners and interest groups",""],[1,"29","10","Strategy Overview to Parliament","Strategy overview to the Riigikogu",""],[1,"29","10","Performance Report Publication","Publishing the performance reports",""],[1,"29","12","Economic Forecast Publication and State Budget Updating","Publishing the economic forecast and updating the state budget, if necessary",""],[1,"29","12","State Budget Presentation to Parliament","Presenting the state budget to the Riigikogu",""],[1,"30","2","Annual Government Presentations to Parliament","At least once a year, each member of the government shall give a presentation in the Riigikogu, providing an overview of the activities in his or her area of responsibility.",""],[1,"30","3","Prime Ministerial Review of Budget Strategy Linkages","The Prime Minister will give a presentation in the Riigikogu after submitting the state budget strategy and the state budget to the parliament, giving an overview of the connections between the changes necessary to achieve the strategic goals of “Estonia 2035” and the planning of state funds.",""],[1,"30","3","Parliamentary Committee Review of State Budget Theses","The review of the state budget is preceded by the introduction of its main theses in the committees of the Riigikogu.",""],[1,"30","4","Annual Government Strategy Review Meetings","Meetings of the Prime Minister and ministers take place every year, where the achievement of the strategic goals of “Estonia 2035” is discussed and the solutions for the necessary changes are discussed.",""],[1,"30","4","Government Strategy Implementation Monitoring","Prior to the state budget strategy meetings, the Strategy Director of the Government Office will give an overview of the state of implementation of “Estonia 2035” at a meeting of the Cabinet of Ministers, highlighting possible bottlenecks in the implementation of the strategy.",""],[1,"30","4","Strategy Bottleneck Resolution Feedback Mechanism","Prior to the discussions on the state budget in the autumn, the Government Office will provide feedback to the members of the government on how the bottlenecks or changes in the strategy discussed in the spring have been resolved and which of them need to be addressed in the state budget.",""],[1,"30","5","Annual Strategy Day for Stakeholder Coordination","Once a year, a strategy day is held with key partners and stakeholders, where an overview of the achievement of the strategy’s goals is provided, the best experiences in addressing development needs are shared and proposals for the implementation of the strategy are made.",""]]}});